 ### PolicyEngine
 
 Hierarchical constraint enforcement system (`bench/cdsfl_registry/`). Five-layer cascade with monotonicity: lower layers cannot weaken higher-layer HARD constraints. Layers: foundation, domain, task, session, model-specific. Not "the registry" (standing correction).
-
-### Quiet arm
-
-The threshold-free side of the two-sided convergence gate: the run must see K consecutive rounds with no new critical finding (default 3) before convergence is permitted. It is the insurance endpoint of the same diminishing-returns curve that gamma measures, and it must agree with the gamma side for the gate to fire — neither alone. Named at `bench/reference_runner_v3.py:1562`. It fires at most once per run, so a per-window rate cannot price it; the relevant figure is the false-quiet chance, measured by `bench/the_false_quiet_rate_is_not_the_gates_rate_2026-10-08.py`.
 
