t had since gained a twin and only `Overnight_Analysis_2026-11-13.txt` was orphaned. **Written as `experimental_notes/Overnight_Analysis_2026-11-13.md`, lint-clean at 0 findings, and RE-RENDERED rather than converted** — the spoken copy carries no markdown, no backticks and no file paths because those are read aloud as noise, so the twin RESTORES the identifiers a reader needs to check any claim. **Orphans since 2026-11-12 are now 0.** The pairing CHECK itself is still owed and belongs in the gate that already verifies a spoken copy is not older than its record. **AND WRITING THAT TWIN EXPOSED A SEPARATE DEFECT IN RULE 32's DETECTOR**, raised and fixed in the same pass because the twin could not be made lint-clean without it: `_ENTRY_IDENT`'s dotted branch read `2.1` out of `2.1.220`, `3.13` out of `3.13.3` and `8.1` out of the section reference `8.1.9.2`, because `.` is a non-word character so `\b` holds on both sides. **158 such fragments across 44 files.** Narrowed, and the narrowing was measured first because it risks FALSE NEGATIVES and accusing is this rule's whole job: **159 of 29,864 matches dropped, 0.005324, Wilson [0.004560, 0.006216], Clopper-Pearson [0.004530, 0.006216], and 0 of the 159 is a genuine entry reference.** 65 of them match a token the task list does define, and all 8 distinct such tokens were read BY EYE rather than trusted to a filter: every one is a dependency version or a 3-component section reference. 12 cases added to the existing guard; the mutation harness now runs **7 of 7 red**, and its own subject list was derived from its mutation table after a 3rd subject raised `KeyError` while its closing line still claimed *both subjects restored*. **HALF 2 — THE WRITER IS NOW NAMEABLE.** What existed was NOT a watcher: `bench/tests/test_tests_do_not_mutate_the_working_tree_2026-08-26.py` is 95 lines of SOURCE-TEXT matching over test files, which `execute-do-not-grep` says asserts only that a module describes itself consistently — it cannot see a write arriving through a route no test file spells out, which is exactly how the 06:27 writer escaped, and B176 records the same guard blind twice over. **A RUNTIME watcher is now in `bench/tests/conftest.py`**, attached to the `pytest_runtest_protocol` hookwrapper that already tracks the current node. **IT ATTRIBUTES BY TIME-SLICE, WHICH IS THE ONLY THING KNOWABLE.** By the time a changed path is noticed the writing process has usually exited and `lsof` on a closed file returns nothing. What IS knowable is which test FILE was executing when the path appeared. **Proved by execution, not by argument: a throwaway git repository with 3 test files, 1 of which writes, and the watcher named `written_by_a_test.txt` against `test_bbb_writes.py` and not against either quiet neighbour.** **THE COST IS MEASURED AND THAT IS WHY IT IS OPT-IN.** `git status --porcelain -uall` costs a mean of 0.1275 s here over 7 runs, median 0.1185 s, so 933 test files is **118.9 s, about 0.0737 of a 1612 s board**. 1 snapshot per TEST across roughly 15,400 tests would be **32.7 minutes** and is refused outright. `CDSFL_WATCH_TREE=1` turns it on for the run that needs it, and a guard asserts a normal board gains **0 lines** — because +7.4 per cent on every commit is not free and his machine is a fixed resource. **AND IT CAN NEVER FAIL A RUN**, which is asserted rather than hoped: driven with `GIT_DIR` pointed at a path that does not exist, the run still exits 0. A watcher that breaks a board is worse than no watcher, because this one exists to EXPLAIN a board rather than to gate it. **Its root is derived from the conftest's own location rather than typed**, which is the hazard `hooks/work_not_narrate.py` still carries and which the `cc2` seat flagged in the 2026-11-14 round: a producer reading a hardcoded root inside a sandbox measures the HOME checkout instead of the tree under review. **P-PASS: `bench/tests/test_the_tree_watcher_names_the_writer_2026-11-14.py`, 4 tests, on `hooks/pre-commit`.** The probe writes into a THROWAWAY repository and never into this one, because a test that dirties the real tree to prove a watcher sees dirty trees is the fault it is testing for. ★★★ **THE OWED PAIRING CHECK IS BUILT 2026-11-22, AND BUILDING IT PROVED THIS ENTRY UNDERSTATES ITS OWN DEFECT BY 2 ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE.** This entry said the check "is still owed"; it is now `bench/tests/test_a_spoken_deliverable_has_a_repository_twin_2026-11-22.py`, 9 tests, ON the gate's GUARDS list. **THE DEFECT RECURRED FIRST, WHICH IS THE ARGUMENT FOR A CHECK OVER A CORRECTION:** the 2 files this entry names gained twins on 2026-11-13 and 2 FRESH orphans appeared on 2026-11-22 -- `The_Ladder_Contained_The_Board_2026-11-22` and `The_Night_The_Instruments_Failed_2026-11-22` -- because nothing checked. Both are now mirrored, and the mirrors are FAITHFUL by an in-process assertion: stripping the heading markers restores the spoken file byte for byte, so a conversion that changed a word fails at render time rather than being found by a reader. **BOTH COPIES ALSO LACKED THE NOTE-STANDARD FOOT-LINE**, which the lint caught on the twin and which was therefore a defect in the DELIVERED text too; added to the Desktop copy and the mirror together, all 4 files now lint at 0 findings. **AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THE GUARD CARRIED A FALSE CLAIM THAT THE GUARD ITSELF CAUGHT ON ITS FIRST RUN.** It asserted every spoken file had a twin, generalising a 10-day window to a folder reaching back to 2026-03-10 -- the window error `feedback_an_aggregate_alarm_must_carry_its_window` records. Measured over the whole folder: **289 of 673 spoken files have no twin, 0.429421, Wilson [0.392528, 0.467114]** on 2 routes agreeing to 5.551e-17, across 89 distinct dates, **8 of them postdating 2026-11-01**. Refusing all 289 would refuse 0.429421 of the archive and teach its reader the checker is noise, which is the reasoning note-standard Rule 30 records for its own baseline -- so they are PINNED AS DATA in `reso